WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.033
-Looking sharp, buddy. -Thank you.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.901
-Thank you for coming onto the show.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:07.801
I want to say, you know, I'm a big fan of Weird Al Yankovic.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.067
I watched "Weird."

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.968
If you haven't seen that documentary,

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.734
mockumentary type of --

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.434
If you haven't seen it, it's super funny.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:17.400
And you pop up as one of my all-time favorites,

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.968
Pee Wee Herman. -There I am.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.968
There I am. It was a little --

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.901
It was a little shocking to see

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.667
how much I actually look like him in real life.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.300
The minute the beard was gone, I was like,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.767
"Oh, yeah, yeah, I can see it."

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.133
-You were fantastic. -Thank you.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.834
-How did you get into that?

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.701
-I begged my way in, was how I -- how I did it.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.334
We were supposed to do a cameo,

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:39.167
the three of us, like, as The Lonely Island.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.467
Like, me, Andy, and Akiva. -Yeah.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:43.367
-And it coincided with Andy having his second child.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.367
Congratulations. -Wow. Yeah...

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.701
[ Cheers and applause ] -Yeah Children!

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.033
And so, unfortunately, like,

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:52.067
it wasn't going to work on the shoot date.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.300
So I called -- I called Weird Al,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.534
and I was like, "Hey, I will do anything to be in this movie.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.801
Like, I'll fly myself out. Whatever."

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.334
-"I'll be anything."

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.901
-And he called me 20 minutes later

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.167
and he was like, "I talked to Eric.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.601
Would you want to be Pee Wee Herman?"

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:08.133
And I was like, "Yeah, yeah. Like, absolutely."

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.868
-Even better. -Yeah.

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.701
-So, did you talk to -- Do you know Paul Reubens?

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.167
-Yes. I do know Paul.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.567
And I was terrified that he was going to hate every --

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:16.901
everything that I was doing.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.300
-Did you call him before you did it?

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.334
-I didn't call him because I was told that I shouldn't.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:22.267
Like, 'cause, they were -- they were trying to have

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.767
everything be a surprise.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:27.200
So, like, I did my thing. It's a short little bit.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.100
-I know, but it works. -But I got to --

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.634
I got to do, you know, the --

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.601
[ Pee Wee Herman laugh ]

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:34.167
-Yeah! That's so good!

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.868
-"Hi!" -It was fantastic.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:38.067
So, let's talk about this. This is a big deal.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.834
I'm so excited to have you on to talk about this.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:41.901
You get to direct not one, but two

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.033
giant Super Bowl commercials.

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:45.534
This is massive. For Pepsi. -Yeah.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.400
-You have -- Dude, you're directing --

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.200
Millions of people are going to see what you directed.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.734
-Yeah. -This is cool.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:53.634
-This is the first time. Because I've made a bunch of movies.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.968
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.300
-And people are actually gonna see this one.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.100
-[ Laughs ] -So that's very exciting.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.834
-There's two up-and-coming stars

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.501
in different -- They're different ads.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:04.167
One is Ben Stiller. The other one is Steve Martin.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.734
-Yes.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:07.067
-Did you know Steve from "Saturday Night Live"?

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:09.334
-I -- I -- There was --

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:13.601
Maybe our worst failure that we've ever had on "SNL"

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.467
was a sketch called "Surf Meeting" that we wrote.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.701
And there was a thing that would happen, like,

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:21.667
when we were at "SNL," where if it would get to a certain point

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:25.100
at night and I'd be laughing a certain way,

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.667
Andy would always be like, "It's not gonna work.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:31.701
Jorm's laughing in that Jorm way. It's not gonna work."

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:34.267
But we wrote this sketch called "Surf Meeting,"

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:37.567
which was a guy -- And it's a group of surfers.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.934
And it's just -- And Andy's running the surf meeting.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:42.567
And he's like, "There's somebody in our crew

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:44.400
that doesn't fit in, you guys.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.167
Like, we don't like him."

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:47.834
And then it just cuts to Steve.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.901
And he's like, "Who is this un-gnarly dude?"

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:54.200
And the thing about "SNL" is that it's moving at such a --

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.601
You know how it is. Like, if you block something

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.701
and it's not working, like, that's it.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.467
You're just like, "Well, that's gonna go to air like that."

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.701
And, like, we were like, "Your time is done."

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.734
And we were like, "This isn't going to work."

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:09.467
-I have a picture of the sketch.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:12.667
-He -- I've got to say. He sold it super hard.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.334
He sold it super hard.

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.501
But between dress and air, I went in to give him, like,

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:18.634
last-minute notes, and he was like,

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:20.067
"It doesn't work, does it?"

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:22.467
And I was like, "No, it doesn't."

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.734
I was like, "Good luck, man." And he was like, "Yeah, sorry."

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:26.100
-At least you were honest with him.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.834
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. -I want to show a teaser clip.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:30.534
Here's a teaser for Jorma's Pepsi Super Bowl commercials.

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:31.901
Take a look at this.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.834
-Hi. I'm Ben Stiller. -And I'm Steve Martin.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:37.200
-As actors, in a way, we never really stop acting.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.734
-For example, Ben is acting right now

00:03:38.734 --> 00:03:41.067
like he's not intimidated standing next to me.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.567
-And Steve's acting like he's not lucky to be here.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.167
-Oh, and Ben's acting like that whole awkward thing he does

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.667
is a character and not his actual personality.

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.634
-And Steve's acting like, "Oh, I'm Steve Martin,"

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:55.033
when really, he's not so -- It's like, okay, we get it.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.467
You're like -- I mean, whatever. You know --

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.100
-See what I mean? -Okay. Banjo player.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.467
-Nepo baby.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:02.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.367
-That's good.

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:06.167
Jorma Taccone, everybody.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.200
-And how about that directing?!

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.934
-No, that directing is what I'm talking about.

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.267
Jorma's Pepsi commercials

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.334
air during the Super Bowl this Sunday on Fox.

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.901
We'll be right back with a performance from Lang Lang.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.801
Stick around, everybody.

